# =============================================================================
# Lab core: identical in every lab repository. Change it in
# vlmurthylab/project-template, not here. Additions and exceptions for this
# repository go in the "This repository" section at the end; later rules win.
# To re-allow a file inside an ignored folder, re-allow the folder first
# (!src/pkg/work/). The PHI check still refuses data file types unless
# phi-guard.conf lists the exact path in ALLOW_FILES.
#
# Lab rule: no subject-level data in GitHub, identified or de-identified,
# including cohort study data. These patterns keep data, secrets and
# regenerable files out automatically; the PHI check (hooks/pre-commit,
# tools/phi_guard.pl) checks what does get committed. Plots, summary results
# and small reference tables are fine to commit.
# =============================================================================

# --- Data folders (never in git) ---------------------------------------------
# raw/ and phi/ anywhere; the others only at the top, so packages can use the
# same names for code (for example src/pkg/work/).
data/*
!data/README.md
raw/
phi/
/derived/
/processed/
/extracts/
/work/

# --- Tabular and statistical data files --------------------------------------
*.csv
*.tsv
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.xlsm
*.ods
*.parquet
*.feather
*.arrow
*.fst
*.sav
*.dta
*.sas7bdat
*.xpt
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.duckdb
*.dump
*.backup
*.pgdump

# --- R -----------------------------------------------------------------------
*.rds
*.rda
*.RData
*.Rdata
*.qs
*.Rout
*.nb.html
*_cache/
_freeze/
.Rhistory
.Rapp.history
.Ruserdata
.Rproj.user/

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.npy
*.npz
*.h5
*.hdf5
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# --- Imaging, ECG and signal files -------------------------------------------
*.dcm
*.nii
*.nii.gz
*.edf
*.hea
*.dat
*.mat

